ke that must stay where it was emitted while the emitter follows the camera or a character.","group":"Speed","name":"AreParticlesRelative"},{"value":"30","type":"Number","unit":"DegreeAngle","label":"Spray cone angle","description":"Spread of the particles around the emission direction, which is the local Z axis of the emitter (upward by default, rotate the instance to aim it). 0 or more than 180 emits in every direction, unless an emission zone radius is set: then 0 emits straight.","group":"Position","name":"SpayConeAngle"},{"value":"0","type":"Number","unit":"Pixel","label":"Emission zone radius","description":"Particles are emitted from a disc of this radius, perpendicular to the emission direction. 0 emits from a single point. Use a large radius (like 1000) for rain or snow falling over a whole area.","group":"Position","name":"ZoneRadius"},{"value":"Additive","type":"Choice","label":"Blending","description":"Additive makes particles glow (fire, magic, energy). Use Normal for rain, snow, smoke or dust. Only applied when the object is created.","group":"Color","choices":[{"label":"Normal","value":"Normal"},{"label":"Additive","value":"Additive"},{"label":"Subtractive","value":"Subtractive"},{"label":"Multiply","value":"Multiply"},{"label":"None","value":"None"}],"name":"Blending"},{"value":"Y-","type":"Choice","label":"Gravity top","description":"Z+: gravity pulls particles down along the Z axis (the usual choice in 3D games). Y-: gravity pulls particles toward Y+.","group":"Speed","choices":[{"label":"Y-","value":"Y-"},{"label":"Z+","value":"Z+"}],"name":"GravityTop"},{"value":"0","type":"Number","unit":"PixelAcceleration","label":"Gravity","description":"Acceleration pulling the particles in the direction given by the gravity top. 0 disables gravity.","group":"Speed","name":"Gravity"},{"value":"true","type":"Boolean","label":"Delete when emission ends","description":"Delete the object once the emission duration is over and every particle disappeared. Uncheck i